C:\TORMENT\TRIOCTAGON_new\wt-ntc-pub01\papers\PAPER_G\README.md:24:The paper separates exact geometry/source identities, the local M2 flip theorem, repaired M3 fixed-parameter capture, and nominal illustrations. M3 retains N=301 and the entrance with squared norm three. M2-to-M3 branch continuation remains unproved. No physical magnetic field, global basin, binary64 theorem, ring robustness, M4 result or X01 adoption is claimed.
C:\TORMENT\TRIOCTAGON_new\wt-ntc-pub01\papers\PAPER_G\README_v0.1.md:6:**LOCAL REVIEW DRAFT.** Prepared for author/scientific review. Not externally peer reviewed; no publication, journal-acceptance or DOI claim. Internal acceptance of M1/M2/repaired M3 does not publish this paper or authorize software changes.
C:\TORMENT\TRIOCTAGON_new\wt-ntc-pub01\papers\PAPER_G\README_v0.1.md:15:The paper proves an exact geometry-attached planar axial construction and finite-step source laws, presents M2's certified local supercritical flip, and separately presents repaired M3's fixed-parameter entrance capture. It preserves the squared-norm-three entrance, direct N=301 inclusion, q<=4789/5000 per two steps, separate H-symmetry certificate and phase-parity summability. **M2-to-M3 branch continuation remains unproved and is not a prerequisite.** Numerical illustrations are explicitly separated from interval certificates and exact algebra. No physical magnetic-field validation, M4, ring development or X01 adoption is claimed.
C:\TORMENT\TRIOCTAGON_new\wt-ntc-pub01\papers\PAPER_G\BUILD_AND_REVIEW.md:11:- [Minimal portable computational supplement](reproducibility/README.md), including actual M2/M3 interval verifiers, exact accepted inputs, final acceptance/correction records and declared I/O adaptations.
C:\TORMENT\TRIOCTAGON_new\wt-ntc-pub01\papers\PAPER_G\BUILD_AND_REVIEW.md:71:M2-to-M3 branch continuation remains unproved and is not required by either theorem. The local M2 theorem supplies no explicit certified positive-mu range. There is no first-entry/global-basin claim, binary64 runtime theorem, lambda=0.5 connection, physical magnetic field validation, X01 adoption or M4 work. Nominal plots are not interval proofs.
C:\TORMENT\TRIOCTAGON_new\wt-ntc-pub01\papers\PAPER_G\BUILD_AND_REVIEW.md:73:No missing controlling M1/M2/repaired-M3 source or new contradiction blocked this draft. The standard contraction theorem was checked in an actual textbook statement; retrieval of Banach's original 1922 text failed, and the [claim map](CLAIM_SOURCE_MAP.md) records that narrow bibliographic limitation. No external literature PDF is redistributed.
